WEBVTT

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.210
Romero, my love...

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.050
What shall I do?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.500
Run away with me, Julietta.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.750
Of course! As far as we must!

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.460
Find the traitors!

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.390
There's no need to let either of them live!

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.920
Once you find them, tear them limb from limb!

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.860
Yes, sir!

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.200
What is it?

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.610
Let's hide in there.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.420
Yes, let's.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.480
Looks like it's morning.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.670
What shall we do, Romero?

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.420
Don't worry, Julietta.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.800
I will protect you.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.700
Romero...

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.760
<i>It's a matter of time until they find us.</i>

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.300
<i>We can't go outside.</i>

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.620
<i>Our pursuers have come too close.</i>

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.650
<i>Isn't there anything... anything we can do?</i>

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.770
<i>I need to at least keep her safe.</i>

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.740
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.680
Wh-What is that? A door?

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.560
Why is there a door?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.340
I'm sure this wasn't here before.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.240
Romero? What is this? 
Do you know something about it?

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.180
I don't.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.930
Hey! I found footsteps!

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.040
They're hiding in this cave!

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.430
Romero...

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.770
It has to be better than staying here!

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.260
Is this a sorcerer's home?

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:53.580
There's clearly some kind of 
teleportation magic involved here.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.380
No! A trap?!

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.640
This light doesn't hurt...

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.270
Whoa... Welcome.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.400
You dropped in awfully early.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.700
<i>He doesn't seem to be a
warrior or a wizard...</i>

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.320
I'm still getting things ready.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.570
Getting ready? What is this place?

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.480
It's an eatery called 
Western Restaurant Nekoya.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.500
Folks from the other world like yourselves

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.490
call it the Restaurant to Another World.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.580
Restaurant to Another World?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.030
You sell food here?

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.720
Yes... but before we get to that...

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.530
You both look awfully pale.
 Are you all right?

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.640
Y-Yes. Don't worry about us.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.770
We were both born like this.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.270
We're quite healthy.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.630
Well, glad to hear it.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:01.900
Would you care to have something 
to eat before you move on?

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.260
We may not look like much, but we're 
quite a reputable establishment.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.530
Romero, we really should eat 
something, shouldn't we?

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.960
Then we'll be customers of this restaurant.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.190
I see... That's true.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.110
Very well. We will eat here.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.600
Then please sit anywhere you'd like.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.300
I'll bring you a menu.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.930
No need.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:34.370
We'd like two servings of the 
most expensive dish you have.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:39.410
Also, if you have a grape liquor as red 
as blood, we'll have that, too.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:44.450
Our most expensive dish would be 
the beefsteak... that is, cooked cow meat.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.690
Is that all right?

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.480
Cooked cow meat, eh?

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:50.200
All right, then.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.670
Bring us that.

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:55.330
Oh, and I'm sorry, 
but neither of us can eat galeo,

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.640
so please don't use any.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.210
Understood. I'll have it 
ready for you shortly.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.470
It looks like we're safe.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.140
Yes, you're right.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:13.660
But if cooked cow meat is 
their most expensive dish...

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.040
It's probably tough and smelly, 
like the sole of a shoe.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.930
Just what kind of restaurant is this?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:26.390
I know. And yet it looks so nice inside.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.930
Oh, well.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.840
It's not as if we ordered food 
because we want to eat it.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.880
I'm so sleepy...

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:40.180
Yes, so am I.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.410
You're both all right with oranie, I assume?

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:51.180
Yes, that's fine.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.460
As long as there's no galeo in it.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.230
It's all right with me, too. Thank you.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.020
Glad to hear it.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:04.020
<i>Beefsteak</i>

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.020
Here is your beefsteak.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.600
<i>What a tremendously appetizing aroma!</i>

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.340
This is cow meat?

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.120
Yes. A friend of mine supplies it.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.510
It's pretty good meat, actually.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.900
And here's the wine, your grape liquor.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:25.540
Thank you.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.890
You get free refills of bread and soup,

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.050
so let me know if you need more.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:39.060
It's nothing like what I had imagined.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.750
Yes, it looks much better than I expected.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.690
Well, then, let's eat.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.710
Yes.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.320
It's so tender!

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:02.450
<i>Is it the way it's processed,
 or is it just naturally good meat?</i>

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:07.790
<i>I can hardly believe something 
this tender could be cow meat!</i>

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:20.000
<i>Goodness! It's amazingly tender!</i>

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.810
<i>The more I chew it, 
the more my mouth is filled</i>

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.810
<i>with the flavors of fat 
and high-quality meat!</i>

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:30.840
<i>The salt added to the meat and the 
hint of spice from the seasonings,</i>

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.710
<i>along with the bite of 
thinly-chopped raw oranie</i>

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.820
<i>and the savoriness of cooked oranie...</i>

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:42.030
<i>The meat juices and sweet fat 
meld together with every bite,</i>

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.690
<i>emphasizing the savory flavor of the meat!</i>

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.640
I can see why it's their most expensive dish.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:52.610
Yes...

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.730
What a refreshing flavor.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.850
How is it so delicious, 
even without being diluted with water?

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:09.100
Oh, you're right! It's truly delicious!

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.730
Running in here was the right choice.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:15.360
Yes, no one can follow us in here.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:19.370
To our future, and a life 
in the dark of night.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:22.570
May the Goddess of Darkness bless us.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:59.320
Excuse me, sir and madam?

00:09:59.590 --> 00:10:01.740
The restaurant is closing now.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.330
Oh...

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.960
I'm so sorry.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.360
Today has been like a miracle.

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:17.550
Thank you for letting us stay so long.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.340
The food was absolutely delicious, 
as was the grape liquor.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.970
Glad to hear it.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.570
The door appears every seven days.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:27.100
Come see us again!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.570
Thank you.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.290
It looks like our pursuers are gone.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.570
Well, let's move on.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.370
If we keep flying through the night,

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.440
we should reach my secret hideout.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:45.950
Okay.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:51.960
If we manage to avoid capture, 
we should visit that restaurant again.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.520
Yes, we should.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:57.710
We owe the people there more 
gratitude than we can say.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.960
And above all, the food was delicious!

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:12.960
Pardon me, Your Highness.

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:26.700
<i>Once every seven days, 
Princess Adelheid goes out for a long walk.</i>

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:30.010
<i>She suddenly disappears,</i>

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:32.620
<i>and I don't see her around the castle.</i>

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:37.990
<i>Is there a secret escape route that 
only the imperial family knows about?</i>

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.730
Mm, still delicious!

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.800
This fried shrimp fills my mouth 
with the scent of the sea!

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.410
I just never get tired of eating it!

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.670
Hello!

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:05.410
Welcome.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.840
Ah, Minced Meat Cutlet!

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:11.600
I haven't seen you in a long time. 
Did you run into some kind of trouble?

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:13.160
Fried Shrimp!

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.460
I just had a little trouble 
deciphering a code, that's all.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.410
Oh? So you gave up and came here?

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:22.840
How rude! I finished the work!

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.220
Very good, then!

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:29.290
I'm ready to order.

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.350
One plate of my usual minced meat cutlet...

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.850
no, make that two plates.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.010
Your order has been accepted.

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:40.590
Two plates just isn't enough 
when it's been so long, eh?

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:42.360
Indeed.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:46.990
But if it goes cold, my delicious 
minced meat cutlets go to waste.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.190
I see.

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:51.650
But there wouldn't be a problem 
with ordering three, would there?

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:56.620
Could you not nitpick everything I do?

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:59.400
I can just order more after I finish one!

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.530
Oh, right! That is one way!

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.010
You should try it.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.890
Welcome!

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:10.890
Hello,

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.070
Princess Adelheid.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.160
I do hope you are well.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.100
Hello, Renner!

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:22.400
Go on, Brother.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.590
R-Right...

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:26.660
I'm glad to see you seem well, Adel...heid.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.660
Same to you, Shareef. You seem quite well.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.420
May we sit with you?

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.420
Yes, by all means!

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.570
One coffee float with soft serve.

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:50.760
I'll have a melon soda float 
with ice cream, please.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.950
Your order has been accepted.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.170
We actually have a gift for you today.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.060
Oh? What is it?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.280
Brother.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:02.940
Right...

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.140
What is it?

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.200
Kaffa beans from the Land of Sand.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.350
From the Land of Sand?

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:15.950
Thank you so much, Shareef and Renner!

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:17.460
I can't wait to try them!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.850
I-I'm glad to hear that.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.570
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:26.460
Here's your coffee float and soda float.

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:29.310
Well, shall we eat?

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:30.150
Yes.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:37.480
Mm... It really is good.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.980
Eating with others makes 
the food taste even better.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:53.250
Well, we should be on our way.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:55.990
Oh, is it that late already?

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.490
It pains me to leave,

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:01.560
b-but I'll look forward to seeing you again.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.500
Yes, I'm looking forward to it, too!

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.430
See you soon, then.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.010
Oh, right!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.020
I wonder if there's a 
dessert I can order to go

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:24.270
that has lots of cream, like a parfait,
 and goes well with kaffa...

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.990
Cream puffs.

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:26.720
Huh?

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:32.530
A dessert made with lots of 
cream that can be ordered to go.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:36.530
If that's what you want, 
I believe cream puffs are ideal.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:38.160
Cream puffs?

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.550
Thank you!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.040
You're welcome.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.310
Excuse me, may I order?

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.180
Sure.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:51.300
I'd like two cream puffs to go, please.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.050
Two of them?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.210
Yes!

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.880
Where could Hannah be?

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:04.920
Hannah!

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:07.450
Huh?! Your Highness?

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:09.360
What are you doing in here?

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.030
I was looking for you.

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:14.780
What? For... me?

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:15.760
Yes.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.070
Please serve these at tea time.

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:20.580
Very well.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:25.140
And what might be inside this box?

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:28.730
A dessert called "cream puffs"
 that contains cream.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.300
A dessert?

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:35.550
Yes. Pudding A La Mode said 
it would go well with kaffa.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.710
<i>"Pudding A La Mode"?</i>

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:42.430
And these are kaffa beans 
from the Land of Sand.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:45.190
Please serve it along with the cream puffs.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:51.930
<i>The Land of Sand? Where did she get these?</i>

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:56.130
Very well. I will take both of these, then.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:57.320
Thank you.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:16:59.940
Oh!

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:04.140
Please make sure there's milk 
and sugar for the kaffa.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.710
Also, there are two cream puffs.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.010
Make sure you bring them both out.

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:10.590
And two kaffas, too!

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.600
All right...

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.600
Your Highness, I've brought 
the kaffa and cream puffs.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.420
Please come in.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:25.170
Pardon me.

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:26.640
Thank you.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.890
Please go ahead and pour the kaffa.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.120
Of course.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.620
<i>Cream Puff</i>

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.570
Those are the cream puffs?

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:49.620
It would seem so.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.390
<i>They seem sort of... plain.</i>

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:55.380
<i>They look more like bread than dessert.</i>

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:04.710
Your kaffa.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:05.800
Thank you.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:07.390
Now, Hannah...

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.150
Please sit in that seat.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:13.260
What?! Oh, no! I mustn't!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:15.900
I could never share a 
table with Your Highness!

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:20.170
Do you... not want to have tea with me?

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.830
N-No, that isn't the case at all!

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.620
<i>What shall I do?</i>

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:32.480
<i>I couldn't refuse and sat 
down without thinking.</i>

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.920
Here you go.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.050
Huh?!

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:43.100
Let's eat them. I can't wait 
to see what they taste like.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.020
Come!

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:45.310
B-But...

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:50.810
Eating with someone else makes food taste 
better than eating alone, doesn't it?

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.900
And have this, too.

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:57.120
It will also taste better 
if we drink it together.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:59.450
Now, let's enjoy our tea time.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.950
A-All right...

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:07.580
Thank you, god of the earth, 
for this, my daily bread.

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:13.180
<i>I can't believe I'm having 
tea with Princess Adelheid.</i>

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:18.460
<i>Huh? For a dessert, it's not too sweet.</i>

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:22.500
<i>The powdered sugar on top 
gives it a bit of sweetness,</i>

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:26.600
<i>but it's not nearly as sweet as 
the desserts I've had before.</i>

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:29.440
<i>What is this?</i>

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:38.210
<i>This white, cloud-like substance...</i>

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:41.650
<i>It has the flavor of milk 
and an elegant sweetness!</i>

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.770
It's delicious.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.910
I'm glad to hear that.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.870
It really is delicious!

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.850
<i>The shell...</i>

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:57.330
<i>Its lack of sweetness actually makes 
it better matched to the filling.</i>

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:00.300
<i>No wonder Princess Adelheid recommended it!</i>

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:04.220
<i>Th-The filling changed?</i>

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.100
<i>Unlike the white stuff,</i>

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.530
<i>this has a rich, deep sweetness.</i>

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:14.740
<i>The light aroma of eggs coming from within 
the smooth texture and milky flavor</i>

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:17.210
<i>brings out the sweetness even more.</i>

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:28.170
<i>This is the most delicious 
dessert I've ever had!</i>

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:39.250
I-I'm sorry! I lost myself 
in Your Highness's presence!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.990
Don't worry about that.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:44.760
I'm happy to see you enjoying it so much.

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:46.920
Now, I'll try mine, too.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.530
Delicious!

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.670
<i>Chocolate parfaits are still delicious,</i>

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.770
<i>but so are cream puffs!</i>

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:05.690
<i>It really does go well 
with the kaffa I received.</i>

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:10.790
<i>I'll have to thank Shareef and Renner.</i>

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:12.790
Huh?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.310
Oh, Hannah...

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.690
Hannah!

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:18.040
Y-Yes?!

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.050
You have cream on your lip.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:31.970
<i>Maybe I should get three 
or four of them next time.</i>

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:44.940
<i>This is the happiest I've seen Princess 
Adelheid since I started living here.</i>

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:49.520
<i>I'm curious to know where 
she got these cream puffs.</i>

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:53.590
<i>But as long as Princess Adelheid is happy,</i>

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:56.120
<i>there's no need for me to know.</i>

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:00.960
This kaffa is very good, too.

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:03.070
Yes, isn't it?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:42.400
<i>Hamburger</i>

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Beef Tendon Curry</i>
